				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt-Qi98YxUtBg8x.webp"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T20:00:53.430Z",
			"content": "<p>DMT is my favorite time zone</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:cjinybngj7dlvspewakwjab2/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzycqm3dus2i",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mindplay.dk/post/3mzycqm3dus2i",
			"author": {
				"name": "Rasmus Schultz",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mindplay.dk",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:cjinybngj7dlvspewakwjab2/bafkreibqgovup3fiqtxmawik2bcsdeap4os7bz7mubvpeg6mmsbokcurve"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T20:46:44.103Z",
			"content": "<p>it's a framework that abstracts the framework. (isn't it?)</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzydajmv7s2o",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:cjinybngj7dlvspewakwjab2/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzycqm3dus2i",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3mzydajmv7s2o",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt-Qi98YxUtBg8x.webp"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T20:55:38.404Z",
			"content": "<p>generically, yes! folks are using it much more specifically than this though</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:gvymykdoxt2ipzpdjd235bbk/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzydre52vs2o",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzya6mtgsc2c",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bnijenhuis.nl/post/3mzydre52vs2o",
			"author": {
				"name": "Bernard Nijenhuis",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bnijenhuis.nl",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:gvymykdoxt2ipzpdjd235bbk/bafkreihbvgk3vwallesr7ekxybhl62jvc7qiqhz2e67jdpmppcpfpeeaf4"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T21:05:03.068Z",
			"content": "<p>No, you're thinking of GMT. DMT was that rapper that used to bark a lot in his songs.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzye5sa2ek2f",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social/post/3mzye5sa2ek2f",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eva Ogbe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/bafkreie24xxgjtxyuq67gsf6dpjx4k775qo4zlqqype2xv7eeswa5ajkqq"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T21:12:00.498Z",
			"content": "<p>It's a framework that's built on top an existing framework. Typically it adds fullstack capabilities to a clientside JS framework. The meta-prefix indicates its relationship to an existing framework. Examples: SvelteKit for Svelte, React Router for React, SolidStart for Solid 1.0, Nuxt for Vue</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzye5sk2ok2f",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzye5sa2ek2f",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social/post/3mzye5sk2ok2f",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eva Ogbe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/bafkreie24xxgjtxyuq67gsf6dpjx4k775qo4zlqqype2xv7eeswa5ajkqq"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T21:12:00.499Z",
			"content": "<p>Can anyone define what exactly a static site is?</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyecb6n3k2f",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzy3bi4ubc2u",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social/post/3mzyecb6n3k2f",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eva Ogbe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/bafkreie24xxgjtxyuq67gsf6dpjx4k775qo4zlqqype2xv7eeswa5ajkqq"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T21:14:30.399Z",
			"content": "<p>Performance for MPAs is better on first load but worse on subsequent loads. Performance for SPAs is worse on first load but better on subsequent loads. Metaframeworks sidestep that entirely. Although there are other tradeoffs</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyff2k46s2t",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:gvymykdoxt2ipzpdjd235bbk/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzydre52vs2o",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3mzyff2k46s2t",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt-Qi98YxUtBg8x.webp"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T21:33:57.840Z",
			"content": "<p>No, you’re thinking of the DMZ, GMT is an inconsistently applied abbreviation for a term describing a color space</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyfkule3s2k",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzye5sk2ok2f",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3mzyfkule3s2k",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt-Qi98YxUtBg8x.webp"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T21:37:12.916Z",
			"content": "<p>yes! that’s an widely agreed upon definition (and it has nothing to do with client JavaScript) 😅😅😅</p>\n<p>it’s a folder full of static files that can be served without any dynamic server/on-request/runtime processing</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyfl7ji722f",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzxz4bpmp22a",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social/post/3mzyfl7ji722f",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eva Ogbe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/bafkreie24xxgjtxyuq67gsf6dpjx4k775qo4zlqqype2xv7eeswa5ajkqq"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T21:37:24.386Z",
			"content": "<p>I may be wrong but I sense this is due to a perception that the e2e benchmark includes only metaframeworks as a means to privilege metaframeworks over other web frameworks instead of in order to compare apples to apples</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyfrolcks2k",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzye5sa2ek2f",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3mzyfrolcks2k",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt-Qi98YxUtBg8x.webp"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T21:41:01.504Z",
			"content": "<p>I’ve seen folks use fullstack, I’ve seen folks say client bundling, component frameworks et al, I’ve seen folks say server runtimes, and the venn diagram here varies</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzykl5pses2q",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyfl7ji722f",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev/post/3mzykl5pses2q",
			"author": {
				"name": "Luca LaValva",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/bafkreigol36dic7ayfuwyurtummesuke3j7zux3k5xs6db6u24anhkmcxe"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T23:06:51.207Z",
			"content": "<p>It is an arbitrary line that they chose, but I agree that there is a difference between the frameworks they evaluated and static site generators</p>\n<p>Whether \"metaframeworks\" is the right terminology is another question, but 11ty &amp; Remix are apples &amp; oranges from my perspective</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:qkk4yywvh3b3qfdr4uhq3ub4/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyl36hm6k2d",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cory.laviska.com/post/3mzyl36hm6k2d",
			"author": {
				"name": "Cory LaViska",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cory.laviska.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:qkk4yywvh3b3qfdr4uhq3ub4/bafkreicdrsy5o7jw2rrtdqvkix6l37zlvmvdri4bvbqgmiri53epbo7xpi"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T23:15:48.858Z",
			"content": "<p>it’s a framework for your framework</p>\n<img src=\"https://static.klipy.com/ii/39f2394ae36df6e199be9eb7c9fa1012/76/54/4xwaLtTl.gif?hh=464&amp;ww=310&amp;mp4=Vjq7nNQkM9D8bDS1WFfg&amp;webm=ivdfZS2TKoHOSaJWVC1\" alt=\"Xzibit Inception Meme\">",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzylgqbuhs2n",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzykl5pses2q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3mzylgqbuhs2n",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt-Qi98YxUtBg8x.webp"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-10T23:22:16.644Z",
			"content": "<p>say more! what is 11ty missing that remix has?</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyqwqyj2c2s",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzylgqbuhs2n",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev/post/3mzyqwqyj2c2s",
			"author": {
				"name": "Luca LaValva",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/bafkreigol36dic7ayfuwyurtummesuke3j7zux3k5xs6db6u24anhkmcxe"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T01:00:42.965Z",
			"content": "<p>The biggest and most obvious gap is on-request architecture, but there are a number of features that client-heavy frameworks have which can't be accomplished in a static site or even in a php app</p>\n<p>Most sites don't need those features, but my hunch is people choose these tools in case one day they do</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyqwrf3fc2s",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyqwqyj2c2s",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev/post/3mzyqwrf3fc2s",
			"author": {
				"name": "Luca LaValva",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/bafkreigol36dic7ayfuwyurtummesuke3j7zux3k5xs6db6u24anhkmcxe"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T01:00:42.966Z",
			"content": "<p>Persistent state across navigations (video player, chat UI) is the one people always point to, most apps never need it but \"what if one day? 🙄\"</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyr3drtis2s",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyqwrf3fc2s",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev/post/3mzyr3drtis2s",
			"author": {
				"name": "Luca LaValva",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/bafkreigol36dic7ayfuwyurtummesuke3j7zux3k5xs6db6u24anhkmcxe"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T01:03:16.888Z",
			"content": "<p>The other **big** difference is that what e18e is calling metaframeworks use a single component model across the server-client boundary, which enables things like end-to-end type safety</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzysftwogc2k",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyr3drtis2s",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3mzysftwogc2k",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt-Qi98YxUtBg8x.webp"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T01:27:03.107Z",
			"content": "<p>this is invaluable feedback, thank you!! I will ruminate on it 🙌🏻</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:avjnsilnwbpskwnwcumwn7c7/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyszax4fc2h",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/stevenspriggs.bsky.social/post/3mzyszax4fc2h",
			"author": {
				"name": "Steven Spriggs",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/stevenspriggs.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:avjnsilnwbpskwnwcumwn7c7/bafkreie4qgjbz5yvahrrca2rz746qxdagc3xvpmzmpfnsmwksdadmuejnq"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T01:37:54.285Z",
			"content": "<p>Zuck’s new framework</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:zjmckaxprnusdgfbfxf3bzoh/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzg4maeyc2b",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzxzxm4ggs2i",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lethalspatula.bsky.social/post/3mzzg4maeyc2b",
			"private": true,
			"date": "2026-11-11T07:19:47.881Z",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzgz7xp222v",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyecb6n3k2f",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mastrojs.bsky.social/post/3mzzgz7xp222v",
			"author": {
				"name": "Mastro.{js,ts}",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mastrojs.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/bafkreicizuiyr3nvt254ufexepmsoerc5gfcpdjg4b43l4hueantbveslm"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T07:35:48.096Z",
			"content": "<p>That was the theory, yes. I wrote a few words about this here: <a href=\"https://mastrojs.github.io/guide/client-side-vs-server-side-javascript-static-vs-ondemand-spa-vs-mpa/\">mastrojs.github.io/guide/client...</a></p>\n<p>And even if that were true, on average users only navigate once (1) after loading the page: <a href=\"https://infrequently.org/2025/11/performance-inequality-gap-2026/#are-spas-working%3F\">infrequently.org/2025/11/perf...</a></p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzirs2uzs2v",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzyr3drtis2s",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mastrojs.bsky.social/post/3mzzirs2uzs2v",
			"author": {
				"name": "Mastro.{js,ts}",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mastrojs.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/bafkreicizuiyr3nvt254ufexepmsoerc5gfcpdjg4b43l4hueantbveslm"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T08:07:26.123Z",
			"content": "<p>nit-pick: these are two independent features. For example, while “Reactive Mastro” can be used to client-side render the same components as core Mastro uses on the server, typesafe APIs without any components are possible as well: <a href=\"https://github.com/mastrojs/api\">github.com/mastrojs/api</a></p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzlbvh3es27",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzgz7xp222v",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social/post/3mzzlbvh3es27",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eva Ogbe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/bafkreie24xxgjtxyuq67gsf6dpjx4k775qo4zlqqype2xv7eeswa5ajkqq"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T08:52:14.023Z",
			"content": "<p>\"The theory behind SPAs was that the client-side JavaScript can do a better job at page navigation than the browser\" <br>\nThat's not how I understand it. The theory behind SPAs is that a site will run faster if you minimize server hops. I don't think these libraries purport to be superior to the browser</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzlbvporc27",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzlbvh3es27",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social/post/3mzzlbvporc27",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eva Ogbe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/bafkreie24xxgjtxyuq67gsf6dpjx4k775qo4zlqqype2xv7eeswa5ajkqq"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T08:52:14.024Z",
			"content": "<p>JS frameworks are still the only cross browser compatible way to get a page with an app-like feel. View transitions are baseline newly available only for same document transitions. Cross document view transitions don't have cross browser support. Speculation rules aren't cross browser either</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzmo4iwvs2y",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzlbvporc27",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mastrojs.bsky.social/post/3mzzmo4iwvs2y",
			"author": {
				"name": "Mastro.{js,ts}",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mastrojs.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/bafkreicizuiyr3nvt254ufexepmsoerc5gfcpdjg4b43l4hueantbveslm"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T09:16:57.817Z",
			"content": "<p>- most SPAs need to do a request to the server to get the next's page data anyway (e.g. getInitialProps)<br>\n- Firefox is in the process of implementing cross-document view transitions. those and speculation rules also fall back gracefully if the browser doesn't support it. it doesn't crash the page!</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzmo5bxos2y",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzmo4iwvs2y",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mastrojs.bsky.social/post/3mzzmo5bxos2y",
			"author": {
				"name": "Mastro.{js,ts}",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mastrojs.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/bafkreicizuiyr3nvt254ufexepmsoerc5gfcpdjg4b43l4hueantbveslm"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T09:16:57.818Z",
			"content": "<p>funny you should mention the app-like feel. at a previous job, we had a Next SPA and wanted to pack it into a native app. the client wanted transitions where the old and new page are visible at the same time – that you can't do with Next. So we added a second webview, effectively making an MPA 😅</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzznwexyhk27",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzykl5pses2q",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social/post/3mzznwexyhk27",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eva Ogbe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/bafkreie24xxgjtxyuq67gsf6dpjx4k775qo4zlqqype2xv7eeswa5ajkqq"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T09:39:28.878Z",
			"content": "<p>I'm just going to admit my ignorance here: how does a static site generator work with a database? In my understanding, once your app needs a database, then it needs a server. Everyone is acting like it's totally obvious that SSGs are just as capable as JS frameworks, but sincerely don't understand</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzznwfgidc27",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzznwexyhk27",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social/post/3mzznwfgidc27",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eva Ogbe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/bafkreie24xxgjtxyuq67gsf6dpjx4k775qo4zlqqype2xv7eeswa5ajkqq"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T09:39:28.879Z",
			"content": "<p>When I say I'm sincere, I truly mean sincere. I feel like I'm missing something huge. Here's what I've heard are the benefits of SSGs:<br>\n- no server vulnerabilities <br>\n- lower bundle size<br>\n- better performance due to lack of JS<br>\n- progressive enhancement<br>\n- embrace browser natives<br>\n- no versioning</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzznwfglb227",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzznwfgidc27",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social/post/3mzznwfglb227",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eva Ogbe",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/evaogbe.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:4q4gbz2leefj42wgosoulqmv/bafkreie24xxgjtxyuq67gsf6dpjx4k775qo4zlqqype2xv7eeswa5ajkqq"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T09:39:28.880Z",
			"content": "<p>If I were making a website with the full feature set of Bluesky, how would I do it with something like 11ty without sacrificing any of those listed benefits?</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3n222ldcwb225",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:zjmckaxprnusdgfbfxf3bzoh/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzg4maeyc2b",
