			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T15:47:48.104Z",
			"content": "<p>This is the important place where PHP isn't a metaframework<br>\n<a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev/post/3mzyr3drtis2s\">bsky.app/profile/lava...</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev/post/3mzyr3drtis2s\">Quoted post</a></p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/app.bsky.feed.post/3n22cycpmuk2o",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:slxmn2ejggkwwbzlej2axmx6/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzirs2uzs2v",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev/post/3n22cycpmuk2o",
			"author": {
				"name": "Luca LaValva",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lavalva.dev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:rvfjpyltvfkaf5ggxaefylft/bafkreigol36dic7ayfuwyurtummesuke3j7zux3k5xs6db6u24anhkmcxe"
			},
			"date": "2026-11-11T15:56:22.195Z",
			"content": "<p>Valid nitpick! My wording could have been better, but a typesafe API isn't the **only** requirement for end-to-end type safety. Full type safety includes typed middlewares, routes, potentially session storage. Not every \"metaframework\" has all of these but they are categorically capable of them</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		}
	],
